# FINN configuration. NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED: with no variables at all FINN runs
# in live mode with the deterministic engine and no LLM.
#
# Locally: copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and uncomment what you need.
# On Vercel: set the same names under Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# Every value is validated when the server starts (src/lib/env.ts); an invalid
# value stops the server with the reason instead of being silently ignored.
# Never commit a real key. .env* files other than this one are git-ignored.

# --- Data mode -------------------------------------------------------------------
# live (default): every screen reads NSE, Yahoo Finance and screener.in, falling back
#   to the committed snapshot in data/snapshot (labelled) when a source fails.
#   Each visitor can still switch their own browser to demo data (header badge or
#   Settings → Data & models) — the path that works when a source is rate-limited.
# demo: every visitor gets the committed capture only; nothing is fetched, rebuilding
#   research is off, and a "Demo data" banner with the capture time shows on every screen.
# Allowed: live | demo
# FINN_DATA_MODE=live

# Which end-of-day price source to try first. Allowed: yahoo | nse-bhavcopy
# (nse-bhavcopy = NSE's official as-traded files; NSE listings only)
# FINN_PRICE_PROVIDER=yahoo

# --- LLM (optional) --------------------------------------------------------------
# Enables two things only: structuring guidance sentences the rule-based parser could
# not, and the cited bull/bear synthesis on the research view. Everything else is
# computed without a model. Server-side only; never exposed to the browser.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model routing: bulk extraction on the cheap tier, synthesis on the strong tier.
# Allowed: any Claude model id (claude-…).
# FINN_MODEL_FAST=claude-haiku-5-5
# FINN_MODEL_REASONING=claude-opus-5-5

# Turn LLM calls off even when a key is present. Allowed: on | off
# FINN_LLM=on

# --- Networking (optional; recommended for a public deployment) --------------------
# How FINN identifies itself to the sources it reads. One line, 8–200 characters.
# Set it to name your deployment with a contact URL; the server warns if a
# production live deployment leaves it unset.
# FINN_USER_AGENT="FINN-prototype/0.1 (+https://github.com/<you>/finn)"

# Where fetched pages, documents and parsed results are cached. Defaults to ./.cache
# locally and /tmp/finn-cache on serverless hosts (Vercel).
# FINN_CACHE_DIR=
